  "question": {
    "text": "For adsorption of a gas on a solid, the plot of log $x / m$ vs log $P$ is linear with slope equal to ( $n$ being whole number)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "CxCDq",
      "text": "$k$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pqfrn",
      "text": "$\\log k$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "etD6U",
      "text": "$n$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "18aSG",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{n}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "According to Freundlich adsorption isotherm, at intermediate pressure, extent of adsorption\n$$\n\\frac{x}{m}=k \\mathrm{P}^{1 / n} \\text { or } \\log \\frac{x}{m}=\\log k+\\frac{1}{n} \\log \\mathrm{P}\n$$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/qIjkRIb8xI5eL_fH_8X4PE7dWlAoqj8xv1nPisc3Cjs.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nplot of $\\log \\frac{x}{m}$ vs log $\\mathrm{P}$ is linear with slope\n$=\\frac{1}{n}$",
    "image": null
  },
